NOTE ON THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS (not part of the license grant above)

This tool runs against libraries you install yourself. Their licenses are
yours to comply with when you distribute a build:

  PyMuPDF (fitz)      AGPL-3.0-only   Linking it into a distributed binary can
                                      trigger AGPL obligations for that binary.
                                      If that is unacceptable, use the
                                      pypdfium2 raster fallback instead
                                      (legal_redactor/formats/pdf_fmt.py ::
                                      PdfRasterFallback); pypdfium2 is
                                      BSD-3-Clause / Apache-2.0.
  rapidocr-onnxruntime Apache-2.0     Bundled PP-OCRv4 model weights are
                                      Apache-2.0.
  OpenCV (opencv-python) Apache-2.0
  numpy / Pillow / lxml / PyYAML      BSD / MIT / HPND
  python-docx           MIT
  openpyxl              MIT
  cryptography          Apache-2.0 / PSF
  pyzipper              Apache-2.0
  typer / rich / click  MIT / BSD-2-Clause

The repository itself does not vendor any of these, nor any model weights.
Test fixtures are generated locally by tests/make_samples.py and contain
synthetic data only; every identifier in them passes real checksum validation
(GB 11643, GB 32100, Luhn) but none refers to a real person.
